---
import Figure from "../Figure.astro";
---
<Figure width="wide" title="What the results cost" sub="Best score so far against cumulative model spend, six runs from scratch.">
  <Fragment slot="controls">
    <span class="seglab">Spend</span>
    <div class="seg" id="cxm"><button data-m="cost" class="on">Dollars</button><button data-m="calls">Model calls</button></div>
  </Fragment>
  <div class="chart" id="cost"></div>
  <div class="legend" id="costleg"></div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <b>Most of the climb costs cents.</b> Height is the number of digits that agree with the best known value, so each
    gridline up is ten times closer. The rest of the budget buys the last digits, where improvements are rare and what
    the system has learned matters most. Hover a line for its final score and spend.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
